# .env.example — per-device settings for panel-api. NOT a code config.
#
# Copy to `.env` on the Pi and fill in. `.env` is gitignored *and* excluded from
# deploy.sh's rsync, so the Pi owns its copy and nothing here ever reaches git:
#
#   scp .env.example mlavinder@delia.local:~/delia/.env
#   ssh mlavinder@delia.local 'chmod 600 ~/delia/.env && nano ~/delia/.env'
#   ssh mlavinder@delia.local 'sudo systemctl restart panel-api'
#
# Loaded by matrix/raspberry_pi/systemd/panel-api.service via
# `EnvironmentFile=-/home/mlavinder/delia/.env` — the leading `-` means the file
# may be absent, so every value below is optional. Missing values degrade one
# feature and never break the panel.
#
# Everything here is either a secret or personal data. That is the whole reason
# this file exists rather than defaults living in the source.

# --- weather overlay --------------------------------------------------------
# Your location, for the 🌡️ overlay (Open-Meteo — no API key, no account).
#
# Deliberately absent from the source: a home latitude/longitude is personal
# data, and anything committed is permanent and public the moment the repo is.
# With these unset the overlay renders "--", the same placeholder it shows when
# the network is down, and logs the reason once at startup.
#
# Find yours: open your area in any map, or `curl 'https://geocoding-api.open-
# meteo.com/v1/search?name=YOUR+CITY&count=1'`. Two decimal places (~1 km) is
# plenty for a temperature and a good deal less identifying than four (~11 m) —
# prefer your city or a nearby landmark over your actual address.
PANEL_WEATHER_LAT=00.00
PANEL_WEATHER_LON=00.00
# fahrenheit | celsius
PANEL_WEATHER_UNIT=fahrenheit

# --- natural-language ask box ----------------------------------------------
# Optional. Without a key /api/ai reports enabled:false and the box renders
# disabled, saying so in its placeholder. Everything else is unaffected.
# Needs `sudo pip3 install --break-system-packages anthropic` on the Pi.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# Tunables: claude-haiku-4-5 is faster and cheaper than the default.
# PANEL_AI_MODEL=claude-opus-5
# PANEL_AI_EFFORT=low
# PANEL_AI_TIMEOUT=60
